<title>NIGERIA: Nigerian 10-day T-bonds sell at three pct.</title>
<headline>Nigerian 10-day T-bonds sell at three pct.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigeria's Central Bank said on Monday it sold 30 million naira worth of 10-day treasury bonds at a weighted average rate of three percent.</p>
<p>Bids totalled the same amount and the true yield will be 3.0025.</p>
<p>Last week the central bank sold 500 million naira worth of 10-day treasury bonds at a weighted average rate of 2.9965 percent.</p>
<p>The central bank also said that on the primary market, 91-day treasury bills worth six billion naira were sold at a marginal rate of 4.5000 percent and true yield of 4.5505 percent. Demand totalled 22.939 billion naira.</p>
<p>($1=80 naira) ((  --Lagos newsroom +234 1 263 03 17))</p>
